    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d654">

                <pb facs="0685" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg587"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.9431/38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-19T17:00:00-05:00">March 19, 1930—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Your telegram 47 dated March 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">18</hi>], 4 p.m.
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">11 a.m.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Does paragraph “No. 6” refer to a general conference of the representatives of
                    creditors or only to representatives of Japanese creditors? Shanghai press
                    despatch relating to the new agreement states that Japan “induced Nanking to
                    reaffirm the Nishihara loans.”<anchor n="24" xml:id="d654-f1"/> Have you any
                    information on this point?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d654-f1" n="24" xml:id="d654-f1-content">
                <p>So-called; they were unsecured Japanese loans to China during the World War.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
